] "\n" [:option {:value "73"} "2024 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "72"} "2026 Winter Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/IHO'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Ice Hockey at the 1932 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "4 – 13 February 1932"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Non-medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "5"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/71"} "James C. Sheffield Speed Skating Oval, Lake Placid"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/77"} "Olympic Arena, Lake Placid"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Until " [:a {:href "/results/20038"} "1928"] ", the Olympic ice hockey tournament had been the only global competition for hockey teams, but, in 1930, the first World Championships were held. In Olympic years, however, the Games would double as the World Championships, a practice that would continue until " [:a {:href "/results/20349"} "1968"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Two rinks were used for the Olympic hockey matches in Lake Placid. Apart from one rink in the centre of the Olympic Stadium, which also hosted the " [:a {:href "/editions/31/sports/SSK"} "speed skating"] ", several matches were held in the " [:a {:href "/venues/77"} "Olympic Arena"] ", marking the first indoor ice hockey matches since " [:a {:href "/results/20000"} "1920"] ". The number of players on the roster had been increased to 14 since 1928, although only 10 could take the bench on any given match. Apart from the official matches, several exhibition matches were played. These also featured two non-national teams: " [:a {:href "/affiliations/3976"} "McGill University"] " (Canada) and " [:a {:href "/affiliations/4583"} "Lake Placid AC"] " (United States)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the main ice hockey tournament, there were only four entered teams (USA, Poland, Germany, and Canada), so a double round-robin was played. This still produced only 12 games, so the organizing committee gave permission for a series of exhibition games to be played, with the four national teams competing against teams from McGill University (Montréal, Québec, Canada), and the Lake Placid Athletic Club, as aforementioned. McGill and Lake Placid each played two scheduled games against the four teams, and then Lake Placid AC faced a team made up players from both the Canadian and American Olympic teams. Both exhibition teams proved powerful, with McGill defeating both the Canadian Olympic Team (2-0) and the USA Olympic Team (2-1), and Lake Placid crushing Germany 6-0, and Poland 6-2. Lake Placid then played a close match against the Canada-USA team, losing 3-2."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/20062"} "Ice Hockey, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "4 – 13 February 1932"] "\n" [:td {} "47"] "\n" [:td {} "4"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n37 (37/0)\n"] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n4 (4/0)\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Non-medal events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/905498"} "Ice Hockey Exhibition (Match #1), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic (non-medal)"] "\n" [:td {} " 5 February 1932"] "\n" [:td {} "24"] "\n" [:td {} "2"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/905499"} "Ice Hockey Exhibition (Match #2), Men"]] 